==Spanish==

===Adjective===
'''americano''' {{m}}, '''americana''' {{f}}
#of the [[America]]s
#of the [[United States]]

===Noun===
'''americano''' {{m}}, '''americana''' {{f}}
#a native of the [[America]]s.
#someone who goes to the United States and then revisits his country after becoming rich.
#a native of the [[United States]].

===Usage notes===
*Definition 1 is the more common meaning.
*In Spain, avoid using '''americano''' to refer only to the United States. Most other Hispanic countries also prefer the use of [[norteamericano]] if the United States is meant.

